            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "This patch assigns the the new opened Session Object to its internal XAResource. Can you test the patch ?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=c_koell",
            "name": "c_koell",
            "key": "c_koell",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Claus K\u00f6ll",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2011-02-22T13:48:28.057+0000",
          "updated": "2011-02-22T13:48:28.057+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12499256/comment/12997923",
          "id": "12997923",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=azschorn",
            "name": "azschorn",
            "key": "azschorn",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Andreas Zschorn",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "i tested it, it does not work, nevertheless we found hopefully a final solution. I will create a patch for it. The TransactionBoundXAResource may not be newly created. This objects are cached by the transaction handler from the application server. So the solution is just to set the session.getXAResource in the TracsactionBoundXAResource. After this everything works as expected.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=azschorn",
            "name": "azschorn",
            "key": "azschorn",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
